WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:04.235
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:04.235 --> 00:00:07.619
Today we're going to talk
about how you can be authentic.

00:00:07.619 --> 00:00:09.147
Rule #4 is our personal favorite,

00:00:09.147 --> 00:00:10.651
and I hope you stick
around to the very end

00:00:10.651 --> 00:00:12.243
for some special bonus clips,

00:00:12.243 --> 00:00:13.627
as well as my take,

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:14.631
and as always, if somebody says something

00:00:14.631 --> 00:00:16.391
that really resonates with you,

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:17.959
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:17.959 --> 00:00:19.599
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:21.292
can be inspired as well.

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:22.125
Enjoy.

00:00:23.932 --> 00:00:27.015
(upbeat happy music)

00:00:40.505 --> 00:00:41.755
- Be authentic.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.723
Be authentic.

00:00:46.988 --> 00:00:50.875
Many people don't even
know what that means.

00:00:50.875 --> 00:00:54.389
It means that you're
clear about who you are.

00:00:54.389 --> 00:00:57.124
You're clear about your
purpose, your protocols,

00:00:57.124 --> 00:00:58.324
and your plans.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.341
You're clear about what you're up to,

00:01:00.341 --> 00:01:04.571
and you speak the truth
of that all the time.

00:01:04.571 --> 00:01:07.339
Be authentic means you're in integrity,

00:01:07.339 --> 00:01:10.870
that what you think, what
you say, what you feel,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.325
and what you do, all matter.

00:01:13.325 --> 00:01:16.237
Now, I know that's hard in Washington,

00:01:16.237 --> 00:01:17.070
(laughter)

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.668
because there's just some
truths you can't tell out here,

00:01:20.668 --> 00:01:23.489
but we want to do the best that we can,

00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:26.322
and when you can't, pray about it.

00:01:27.507 --> 00:01:28.636
But be authentic.

00:01:28.636 --> 00:01:31.562
So many of us don't allow people

00:01:31.562 --> 00:01:33.546
to know who we are.

00:01:33.546 --> 00:01:35.379
As I travel around this country,

00:01:35.379 --> 00:01:38.514
I meet people all over the country

00:01:38.514 --> 00:01:40.847
who are suffering in silence

00:01:43.101 --> 00:01:45.629
because they're not authentic about

00:01:45.629 --> 00:01:48.744
what they need, what they want,

00:01:48.744 --> 00:01:52.577
what they're doing, what
they're experiencing.

00:01:56.087 --> 00:01:57.734
- Every decision we make in our lives,

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:01.147
as individuals, or as organizations,

00:02:01.147 --> 00:02:02.540
is a piece of communication.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.109
It's our way of saying
something about who we are,

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:06.594
and what we believe.

00:02:06.594 --> 00:02:09.034
This is why authenticity matters.

00:02:09.034 --> 00:02:11.891
This is why you have to
say and do the things

00:02:11.891 --> 00:02:13.770
you actually believe

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.687
because the things you
say and do are symbols

00:02:17.687 --> 00:02:19.303
of who you are,

00:02:19.303 --> 00:02:20.799
and we look for those symbols

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:23.239
so we can find people who
believe what we believe.

00:02:23.239 --> 00:02:25.231
Our very survival depends on it,

00:02:25.231 --> 00:02:26.687
so if you're putting out false symbols,

00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:28.799
you will attract people to those symbols,

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:31.921
but you won't be able
to form trust with them.

00:02:31.921 --> 00:02:33.888
This is what Tiger Woods did to us.

00:02:33.888 --> 00:02:35.391
He lied.

00:02:35.391 --> 00:02:36.632
He lied.

00:02:36.632 --> 00:02:40.228
He told us what he thought
that we wanted to hear,

00:02:40.228 --> 00:02:42.427
and it was great, and we were drawn to it,

00:02:42.427 --> 00:02:44.252
and all of us who kind of liked that idea

00:02:44.252 --> 00:02:46.331
of sort of the good guy

00:02:46.331 --> 00:02:47.532
were drawn to it,

00:02:47.532 --> 00:02:50.339
until we found out it was a lie.

00:02:50.339 --> 00:02:51.915
He could have been the bad boy of golf.

00:02:51.915 --> 00:02:54.468
He could have had all
the same endorsements,

00:02:54.468 --> 00:02:55.699
and had a fantastic career,

00:02:55.699 --> 00:02:57.542
and still been hailed as one of the great

00:02:57.542 --> 00:02:59.333
athletes of our day,

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.166
but he didn't.

00:03:00.166 --> 00:03:01.445
He chose to lie.

00:03:01.445 --> 00:03:03.613
Good luck forming trust again, Tiger.

00:03:03.613 --> 00:03:05.117
We don't believe you.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:07.285
We don't trust you.

00:03:07.285 --> 00:03:09.405
The goal of putting something out there,

00:03:09.405 --> 00:03:10.973
if you say what you believe,

00:03:10.973 --> 00:03:12.109
and you do what you believe,

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:15.093
you will attract people who
believe what you believe.

00:03:15.093 --> 00:03:16.793
If you go to one of your friends,

00:03:16.793 --> 00:03:19.025
and you say to one of your friends,

00:03:19.025 --> 00:03:21.529
"How would you like me to dress"

00:03:21.529 --> 00:03:22.362
"so that you'll like me better?"

00:03:22.362 --> 00:03:25.233
"How would you want me to address you?"

00:03:25.233 --> 00:03:29.701
"How do you want me to speak
so that you'll like me more?"

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:30.534
Right?

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:32.064
You're friends are going
to look at you and be like,

00:03:32.064 --> 00:03:34.015
"What are you talking about?"

00:03:34.015 --> 00:03:36.615
"Come on, come on, come
on, what should I wear"

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.791
"so that you'll find me more appealing,"

00:03:38.791 --> 00:03:40.320
"and how would you like
me to speak to you,"

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.921
"so that you'll like me more?"

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.680
Your friends are going to tell you,

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.401
"Just be yourself."

00:03:45.401 --> 00:03:46.449
"That's why I like you."

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:47.282
"I don't care ..."

00:03:47.282 --> 00:03:48.329
"Just be yourself."

00:03:48.329 --> 00:03:50.281
Now think about what we do in industry.

00:03:50.281 --> 00:03:51.114
What do we do?

00:03:51.114 --> 00:03:51.947
We do market research,

00:03:51.947 --> 00:03:53.496
and we go out and we ask the customers,

00:03:53.496 --> 00:03:54.673
"What kind of things, the way we ..."

00:03:54.673 --> 00:03:56.319
"What style should we speak to you?"

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:57.474
"How should we decorate ourselves?"

00:03:57.474 --> 00:03:58.920
"What kind of things are you drawn to"

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.728
"so that we can do those
things so you'll like us more."

00:04:00.728 --> 00:04:02.776
It's just as ridiculous.

00:04:02.776 --> 00:04:04.368
It's just as ridiculous.

00:04:04.368 --> 00:04:06.416
Organizations should say and do the things

00:04:06.416 --> 00:04:08.080
they actually believe,

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.280
and they will attract people

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.008
who believe what they believe,

00:04:11.008 --> 00:04:12.817
or they can choose to lie,

00:04:12.817 --> 00:04:14.368
and at the slightest hint

00:04:14.368 --> 00:04:16.632
that they might be lying,

00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:18.176
cynicism sets in,

00:04:18.176 --> 00:04:19.624
and people start saying, "I'm not sure"

00:04:19.624 --> 00:04:21.408
"I can trust these guys"

00:04:21.408 --> 00:04:23.048
"because there's not a lot of consistency"

00:04:23.048 --> 00:04:24.393
"in all the things they say and do"

00:04:24.393 --> 00:04:26.889
"which means they can't have
a very strong belief set,"

00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:29.457
"or they're lying to me."

00:04:29.457 --> 00:04:31.247
We call them inauthentic.

00:04:31.247 --> 00:04:33.095
The entire process of asking other people

00:04:33.095 --> 00:04:34.983
who we should be is inauthentic.

00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:36.822
That's hilarious to me.

00:04:36.822 --> 00:04:39.495
All these positioning studies
we do are inherent ...

00:04:39.495 --> 00:04:40.991
"We're going to do a study
to find out from people"

00:04:40.991 --> 00:04:42.479
"so we can be more authentic."

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:43.991
That's hilarious.

00:04:43.991 --> 00:04:45.591
(audience laughing)

00:04:45.591 --> 00:04:46.972
Say and do what you actually believe

00:04:46.972 --> 00:04:48.868
and the symbols you put out there,

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:50.068
the things you say and the things you do,

00:04:50.068 --> 00:04:53.395
those red hats, are ways
that people can find you.

00:04:53.395 --> 00:04:56.267
- Are you always editing your life?

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:58.155
Look, that bird is singing up there,

00:04:58.155 --> 00:04:59.115
(bird noises)

00:04:59.115 --> 00:04:59.948
Right?

00:04:59.948 --> 00:05:02.331
It's not editing its
life, it's just doing it.

00:05:02.331 --> 00:05:04.955
There is no stop button in life.

00:05:04.955 --> 00:05:08.379
There is no rewind button in life.

00:05:08.379 --> 00:05:11.395
If you fall down, well, you fall down.

00:05:11.395 --> 00:05:12.228
You got to get back up.

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:13.723
You can't say, "Cut."

00:05:13.723 --> 00:05:15.595
"Let's do that again."

00:05:15.595 --> 00:05:16.563
It happened.

00:05:16.563 --> 00:05:18.267
There is no rehearsal,

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:20.267
so on a practical level,

00:05:22.643 --> 00:05:25.427
I remind myself that I
don't have to use a filter

00:05:25.427 --> 00:05:27.677
every time I post a selfie.

00:05:28.954 --> 00:05:31.704
How I am, surely, is good enough.

00:05:33.763 --> 00:05:36.411
Once I reminded myself of that,

00:05:36.411 --> 00:05:39.744
I started to live a more authentic life.

00:05:41.144 --> 00:05:42.227
Less editing,

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.393
more improvising,

00:05:46.242 --> 00:05:48.825
more being in the here and now.

00:05:49.845 --> 00:05:51.213
- To be authentic,

00:05:51.213 --> 00:05:53.341
we have to be super, super present

00:05:53.341 --> 00:05:55.995
and aware in every
conversation that we have,

00:05:55.995 --> 00:05:58.240
so I encourage you next time you go out

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.082
to a lunch or a dinner with your friends,

00:06:00.082 --> 00:06:02.410
put your cell phone
down, and actually listen

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.769
because that's what a
highly authentic person

00:06:04.769 --> 00:06:07.856
would do is just to be
fully present in the moment.

00:06:07.856 --> 00:06:10.536
The highly authentic person
is truly retrospective,

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.899
and what I mean by that is they're always

00:06:11.899 --> 00:06:13.965
looking back at the week,

00:06:13.965 --> 00:06:15.957
they're always looking back two weeks,

00:06:15.957 --> 00:06:17.596
and they're seeing lessons
that they've learned.

00:06:17.596 --> 00:06:18.772
They're journaling.

00:06:18.772 --> 00:06:21.804
They're really trying to
understand what happened,

00:06:21.804 --> 00:06:24.260
and how to make it better
in the present moment.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.612
They're not looking back
from a painful sense,

00:06:26.612 --> 00:06:27.445
you know, the pain body,

00:06:27.445 --> 00:06:28.614
as Eckhart Tolle would talk about,

00:06:28.614 --> 00:06:30.140
but they're looking back at it

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.732
from a sense of what can I
learn from this experience,

00:06:32.732 --> 00:06:34.569
so that they can transcend
that vicious circle,

00:06:34.569 --> 00:06:36.714
that monkey mind, or whatever they're in,

00:06:36.714 --> 00:06:39.483
and lead to a higher
level in their own life.

00:06:39.483 --> 00:06:40.857
The reason for doing this is often

00:06:40.857 --> 00:06:42.929
to impact other people.

00:06:42.929 --> 00:06:44.846
- Greatness is not this

00:06:46.344 --> 00:06:48.761
wonderful, esoteric, elusive,

00:06:50.511 --> 00:06:52.261
God-like feature that

00:06:53.256 --> 00:06:58.089
only the special among us
will ever taste, you know.

00:06:58.089 --> 00:07:01.947
It's something that truly
exists in all of us.

00:07:01.947 --> 00:07:03.364
It's very simple.

00:07:04.803 --> 00:07:07.092
This is what I believe,

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:09.606
and I'm willing to die for it.

00:07:09.606 --> 00:07:10.689
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:07:10.689 --> 00:07:12.243
- Period.

00:07:12.243 --> 00:07:13.076
It's that simple.

00:07:13.076 --> 00:07:14.670
- I know who I am and
I know what I believe.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.408
- I know who I am, I know what I believe.

00:07:16.408 --> 00:07:17.241
- That's all I need to know.

00:07:17.241 --> 00:07:18.800
- And that's all I need to know,

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.024
so from there, you do what you need to do.

00:07:21.024 --> 00:07:23.040
- You don't need everyone to like you,

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.777
and in fact, it's not even possible

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:25.722
to make everyone like you,

00:07:25.722 --> 00:07:27.016
even if you do everything perfectly,

00:07:27.016 --> 00:07:28.776
so you have to just
accept that certain people

00:07:28.776 --> 00:07:32.691
will not like you, and that
it doesn't really matter.

00:07:32.691 --> 00:07:37.440
In fact, your best strategy
and chances at success in life,

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:38.544
chances at fulfillment,

00:07:38.544 --> 00:07:40.592
and chances at the most people liking you

00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:42.144
is to be yourself

00:07:42.144 --> 00:07:44.521
because when you're yourself,
your authentic self,

00:07:44.521 --> 00:07:46.065
you're magnetic.

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:46.898
You're attractive.

00:07:46.898 --> 00:07:47.731
People want to be near you,

00:07:47.731 --> 00:07:49.729
maybe not the same people
that want to be near

00:07:49.729 --> 00:07:51.425
your fake self right now,

00:07:51.425 --> 00:07:53.906
so acknowledge that.

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:55.849
I'm not saying that you
can maintain everything

00:07:55.849 --> 00:07:57.819
in your life as it is,
and still be yourself.

00:07:57.819 --> 00:07:59.444
You might need to make some sacrifices.

00:07:59.444 --> 00:08:01.212
There might be some costs

00:08:01.212 --> 00:08:03.079
because chances are, right now,
you've whored yourself out,

00:08:03.079 --> 00:08:05.380
and now you have some social debts, right?

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.251
When I tell you to stop
caring about other people,

00:08:08.251 --> 00:08:09.220
and start being authentic,

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.803
well, you're going to come
up with all sorts of reasons

00:08:10.803 --> 00:08:13.170
about why that's too costly for you.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.251
You're going to say, "Well,
then my boss will say"

00:08:15.251 --> 00:08:16.314
"something bad."

00:08:16.314 --> 00:08:17.787
"My job might be in danger."

00:08:17.787 --> 00:08:19.651
"My relationship might be in danger."

00:08:19.651 --> 00:08:21.571
"Somebody else might be in danger."

00:08:21.571 --> 00:08:24.466
Well, what's more important to you?

00:08:24.466 --> 00:08:25.948
Is it more important for you

00:08:25.948 --> 00:08:28.691
to be getting those shallow things,

00:08:28.691 --> 00:08:31.370
or is it more important for
you to be self-expressive,

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.210
to really be yourself, to
really be fulfilled inside,

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:35.443
and then, to act from that,

00:08:35.443 --> 00:08:36.972
and to live your life from that,

00:08:36.972 --> 00:08:38.643
and to create a business from that place,

00:08:38.643 --> 00:08:40.179
to create a career from that place,

00:08:40.179 --> 00:08:44.645
to create a nice
relationship from that place?

00:08:44.645 --> 00:08:46.478
What's more important?

00:08:47.469 --> 00:08:49.518
I mean, you can still
keep whoring yourself out

00:08:49.518 --> 00:08:50.693
if you want to,

00:08:50.693 --> 00:08:52.941
but in the end, being a
whore is not a good way

00:08:52.941 --> 00:08:54.524
to go through life,

00:08:55.445 --> 00:08:58.301
so my suggestion is to bite
the bullet on this one,

00:08:58.301 --> 00:09:01.134
and be yourself despite the costs.

00:09:03.527 --> 00:09:07.015
In fact, what I'll have you do is ...

00:09:07.015 --> 00:09:09.201
We're going to wrap with
this, something practical.

00:09:09.201 --> 00:09:12.367
I want you to write down
a list of all the ways,

00:09:12.367 --> 00:09:14.056
and all the areas in your life,

00:09:14.056 --> 00:09:16.311
where if you started
to really act yourself,

00:09:16.311 --> 00:09:18.912
really honest with yourself,

00:09:18.912 --> 00:09:20.575
and expressing yourself honestly,

00:09:20.575 --> 00:09:22.503
where you might incur some costs,

00:09:22.503 --> 00:09:24.368
where there might be some
friction and some tension.

00:09:24.368 --> 00:09:27.550
What are those debts that
you're now kind of sunk into?

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:29.118
I want you to write those down,

00:09:29.118 --> 00:09:30.782
at work, in your relationship,

00:09:30.782 --> 00:09:32.303
you know, in any kind of
interaction you're having

00:09:32.303 --> 00:09:34.510
with other people,

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.590
any area of life.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.895
Write them down.

00:09:36.895 --> 00:09:40.046
Maybe you think that you'll
have strain in your marriage.

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.566
Maybe you'll think you'll
have strain at work,

00:09:41.566 --> 00:09:42.399
so write those down,

00:09:42.399 --> 00:09:44.091
and be specific about what the costs are,

00:09:44.091 --> 00:09:47.211
and then, when you survey
the whole list of costs,

00:09:47.211 --> 00:09:49.242
I want you to say,

00:09:49.242 --> 00:09:52.075
"Am I satisfied with these costs,"

00:09:52.952 --> 00:09:55.385
"or am I going to decide
to be my authentic self"

00:09:55.385 --> 00:09:56.550
"despite the costs?"

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:57.583
Fuck the costs.

00:09:57.583 --> 00:09:58.583
Be yourself.

00:10:00.022 --> 00:10:01.710
You're going to be much happier,

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.647
and, ultimately, you're going
to be more successful too.

00:10:03.647 --> 00:10:05.521
It just might take a while for you

00:10:05.521 --> 00:10:07.629
to recreate your life a little bit

00:10:07.629 --> 00:10:09.077
because some of those things
might actually fall off ...

00:10:09.077 --> 00:10:11.437
You know, out of your life,

00:10:11.437 --> 00:10:13.021
and when they do, you
have to be okay with it

00:10:13.021 --> 00:10:14.485
because you have to recognize that

00:10:14.485 --> 00:10:15.661
when you are your authentic self,

00:10:15.661 --> 00:10:16.494
now people ...

00:10:16.494 --> 00:10:17.327
It's going to be better.

00:10:17.327 --> 00:10:18.834
It's going to be more of a stable success

00:10:18.834 --> 00:10:21.096
because now people that are
going to be attracted to you,

00:10:21.096 --> 00:10:23.137
and situations that you're
going to be involved in,

00:10:23.137 --> 00:10:24.632
those are going to be more authentic.

00:10:24.632 --> 00:10:27.032
They're going to be
aligned with you, right,

00:10:27.032 --> 00:10:29.568
rather than being the sham
that they are right now,

00:10:29.568 --> 00:10:33.164
so you got to stop living
this sham kind of life.

00:10:33.164 --> 00:10:35.652
The final exercise that
I'm going to wrap on,

00:10:35.652 --> 00:10:36.628
is the following.

00:10:36.628 --> 00:10:40.429
I want you to observe
yourself over the next day.

00:10:40.429 --> 00:10:42.078
In very subtle ways,

00:10:42.078 --> 00:10:44.038
I want to you to see how
you're whoring yourself out,

00:10:44.038 --> 00:10:46.119
and I want you to call yourself out on it.

00:10:46.119 --> 00:10:48.054
For example, if someone sends you

00:10:48.054 --> 00:10:49.430
a simple little email,

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.870
and you want to reply to it,

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.798
but then, all of the sudden
you kind of stop yourself,

00:10:52.798 --> 00:10:55.878
and your natural reply,
you want to kind of a,

00:10:55.878 --> 00:10:57.238
you know, you want to
soften the edges of it.

00:10:57.238 --> 00:10:59.398
You don't want to be
coming off too impolite,

00:10:59.398 --> 00:11:01.172
or too rude, or you're worried about

00:11:01.172 --> 00:11:02.863
what that other person is going to,

00:11:02.863 --> 00:11:05.199
how he's going to interpret your response,

00:11:05.199 --> 00:11:07.527
and you kind of dumb down your response

00:11:07.527 --> 00:11:08.631
on that email,

00:11:08.631 --> 00:11:10.911
make it kind of sweet and polite.

00:11:10.911 --> 00:11:11.903
Well, notice that.

00:11:11.903 --> 00:11:12.975
Notice what you're doing there

00:11:12.975 --> 00:11:14.607
is that you are whoring yourself out

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:17.002
to get a positive
reaction from that person.

00:11:17.002 --> 00:11:19.367
At that point, I don't
want you to judge yourself.

00:11:19.367 --> 00:11:20.399
This is kind of mindfulness.

00:11:20.399 --> 00:11:22.231
I also have a video on
mindfulness you want to check out.

00:11:22.231 --> 00:11:24.583
This is practicing mindfulness

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:28.808
is you just observe yourself
whoring yourself out,

00:11:28.808 --> 00:11:30.888
and you don't judge yourself.

00:11:30.888 --> 00:11:32.200
You don't say this is bad or good,

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.672
you just let it be,

00:11:33.672 --> 00:11:34.657
and you just follow through.

00:11:34.657 --> 00:11:35.490
Carry it through.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.512
Whore yourself out,

00:11:36.512 --> 00:11:37.873
but be conscious.

00:11:37.873 --> 00:11:39.281
This time, do it consciously,

00:11:39.281 --> 00:11:40.784
and I want you to do
that for the whole day,

00:11:40.784 --> 00:11:43.552
and notice the subtle little
ways in which you're doing it.

00:11:43.552 --> 00:11:44.481
- So my take on this is

00:11:44.481 --> 00:11:46.184
if you want to be authentic,

00:11:46.184 --> 00:11:48.615
then you have to understand
that you are unique.

00:11:48.615 --> 00:11:50.150
You have something special.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.006
You have a gift.

00:11:51.006 --> 00:11:51.839
You have a voice.

00:11:51.839 --> 00:11:54.510
You have something that is
different and special and unique

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:56.446
about you and it's okay,

00:11:56.446 --> 00:11:57.423
and that's a good thing.

00:11:57.423 --> 00:11:59.726
I think too many people
are trying to fit in.

00:11:59.726 --> 00:12:01.374
Too many people worry about
what other people think

00:12:01.374 --> 00:12:02.207
about them.

00:12:02.207 --> 00:12:04.158
Too many people are trying
to live a life according

00:12:04.158 --> 00:12:06.646
to other people's expectations
instead of their own.

00:12:06.646 --> 00:12:08.166
You have your own voice,

00:12:08.166 --> 00:12:09.382
and in order to be authentic,

00:12:09.382 --> 00:12:12.070
before even worrying about
being authentic for others,

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:13.894
you need to be authentic to yourself,

00:12:13.894 --> 00:12:15.598
and learning to listen
to that little voice,

00:12:15.598 --> 00:12:17.254
learning to trust that little voice,

00:12:17.254 --> 00:12:19.190
learning that when you
have this crazy idea

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:21.550
for something that you
want to try or do or say,

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.094
that you do it,

00:12:23.094 --> 00:12:24.286
even in some small way.

00:12:24.286 --> 00:12:25.422
You let go of the fear.

00:12:25.422 --> 00:12:26.591
You let go of the fear of failure.

00:12:26.591 --> 00:12:27.886
You let go of the fear of judgement.

00:12:27.886 --> 00:12:30.094
Let go of any fears
that you have around it,

00:12:30.094 --> 00:12:32.102
and just go out and do something about it.

00:12:32.102 --> 00:12:34.270
The more you get used to trusting

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.950
that little voice inside your head,

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:38.183
the more you get used to
when you get that idea,

00:12:38.183 --> 00:12:40.118
actually doing something about it,

00:12:40.118 --> 00:12:43.126
then you'll start to live
a much more authentic life

00:12:43.126 --> 00:12:45.478
instead of a cookie cutter life version

00:12:45.478 --> 00:12:47.112
that somebody else has created for you.

00:12:47.112 --> 00:12:49.209
So I believe that it starts with you.

00:12:49.209 --> 00:12:52.152
It starts by trusting yourself more.

00:12:52.152 --> 00:12:54.457
It starts by saying yes to things more.

00:12:54.457 --> 00:12:57.248
It starts by not bowing down to fear more.

00:12:57.248 --> 00:12:59.672
You need to be authentic
to yourself first.

00:12:59.672 --> 00:13:01.762
From there, it's having the courage

00:13:01.762 --> 00:13:04.168
to be authentic in every situation.

00:13:04.168 --> 00:13:05.216
There was this really great clip

00:13:05.216 --> 00:13:07.480
of Warren Buffett and Jay Z,

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.216
they're being interviewed
by Forbes magazine,

00:13:09.216 --> 00:13:12.015
and they asked Jay Z if
he's ever intimidated

00:13:12.015 --> 00:13:14.129
when he walks into these
business boardrooms

00:13:14.129 --> 00:13:15.633
because that wasn't how he grew up,

00:13:15.633 --> 00:13:16.831
and he said something like--

00:13:16.831 --> 00:13:19.159
- This is who I am, you know.

00:13:19.159 --> 00:13:20.415
This is what I do.

00:13:20.415 --> 00:13:21.981
- What I always feel that
I liked about that clip is

00:13:21.981 --> 00:13:25.053
here is a guy who is unafraid
to always be himself,

00:13:25.053 --> 00:13:26.694
even when he's in a room

00:13:26.694 --> 00:13:28.821
that he may not have ever been in before.

00:13:28.821 --> 00:13:30.325
How many times are you in a situation

00:13:30.325 --> 00:13:31.812
that you've never been in before,

00:13:31.812 --> 00:13:35.045
and you have the pressure
to act according to

00:13:35.045 --> 00:13:38.528
the rules instead of acting according

00:13:38.528 --> 00:13:40.191
to how you wanted to act?

00:13:40.191 --> 00:13:43.233
I think the more confident
that you are in yourself,

00:13:43.233 --> 00:13:45.159
the more authentic you believe you are

00:13:45.159 --> 00:13:46.271
to yourself,

00:13:46.271 --> 00:13:48.997
then the easier it is to
express that outwards.

00:13:48.997 --> 00:13:50.837
When you have full confidence in yourself

00:13:50.837 --> 00:13:52.407
with who you are and what you want to do,

00:13:52.407 --> 00:13:55.333
then, suddenly, other people's opinions,

00:13:55.333 --> 00:13:56.541
they don't matter as much.

00:13:56.541 --> 00:13:57.925
When you don't know what you do,

00:13:57.925 --> 00:13:58.917
when you are afraid,

00:13:58.917 --> 00:14:01.173
when you don't have that
level of self-awareness

00:14:01.173 --> 00:14:03.111
and self-confidence, and
finding your one word

00:14:03.111 --> 00:14:04.285
can really help you in that,

00:14:04.285 --> 00:14:05.989
then that's when you get
ruled by other people,

00:14:05.989 --> 00:14:07.269
and that's when you are afraid,

00:14:07.269 --> 00:14:08.343
and that's when you say no to things

00:14:08.343 --> 00:14:09.741
that could be really helpful to you.

00:14:09.741 --> 00:14:11.109
That's when you don't
take those opportunities

00:14:11.109 --> 00:14:11.942
that you should.

00:14:11.942 --> 00:14:13.078
Those are my suggestions,

00:14:13.078 --> 00:14:18.050
and I'm really curious to
figure out what you guys think.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:19.154
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:19.154 --> 00:14:19.987
I'd love to know,

00:14:19.987 --> 00:14:23.056
what challenges do you
have in being authentic.

00:14:23.056 --> 00:14:24.722
Please leave it in the comments below.

00:14:24.722 --> 00:14:26.121
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:14:26.121 --> 00:14:27.664
I made this episode of Believe Life

00:14:27.664 --> 00:14:29.824
because Dax Miller asked me to,

00:14:29.824 --> 00:14:31.216
so if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:14:31.216 --> 00:14:32.745
in the next Believe Life,

00:14:32.745 --> 00:14:34.247
please leave it in the comments below,

00:14:34.247 --> 00:14:35.223
and I'll see what I can do.

00:14:35.223 --> 00:14:36.574
I'd also love to know which of the clips

00:14:36.574 --> 00:14:38.071
resonated the most with you and why?

00:14:38.071 --> 00:14:39.535
What did you take from this video

00:14:39.535 --> 00:14:41.592
that you're going to apply to
your life or your business?

00:14:41.592 --> 00:14:43.112
Please leave it in the comments below,

00:14:43.112 --> 00:14:44.791
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:14:44.791 --> 00:14:46.037
Finally, I wanted to
give a quick shout out

00:14:46.037 --> 00:14:47.389
to Christophe Logiste.

00:14:47.389 --> 00:14:49.605
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:14:49.605 --> 00:14:51.629
and for tweeting that awesome picture out.

00:14:51.629 --> 00:14:53.285
I really, really appreciate it, man.

00:14:53.285 --> 00:14:54.765
Thank you guys, again, for watching.

00:14:54.765 --> 00:14:55.709
I believe in you.

00:14:55.709 --> 00:14:57.893
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:14:57.893 --> 00:14:59.814
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:59.814 --> 00:15:01.165
Much love.

00:15:01.165 --> 00:15:02.665
I'll see you soon.

00:15:08.527 --> 00:15:11.565
- I think over time, people
develop their own signature,

00:15:11.565 --> 00:15:13.093
and I think it takes a while to find out

00:15:13.093 --> 00:15:15.077
what your signature really is.

00:15:15.077 --> 00:15:16.350
I'll fast forward a little bit.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.301
Where I am now, we never
really marketed ourselves.

00:15:19.301 --> 00:15:20.797
As I began to build a little company

00:15:20.797 --> 00:15:22.197
around the success of the book,

00:15:22.197 --> 00:15:23.989
and I brought in other
trainers and coaches

00:15:23.989 --> 00:15:25.229
and presenters,

00:15:25.229 --> 00:15:27.200
and started to build
some product around that.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.737
Still not a huge company.

00:15:28.737 --> 00:15:30.512
I mean, there are only 20 plus of us,

00:15:30.512 --> 00:15:32.322
you know, doing that work,

00:15:32.322 --> 00:15:34.088
but we're partnering with
other people out there,

00:15:34.088 --> 00:15:36.049
but as I started to do that,

00:15:36.049 --> 00:15:38.421
we really realized that the
brand had kind of run out

00:15:38.421 --> 00:15:39.254
from under us.

00:15:39.254 --> 00:15:41.550
GTD, which was the shorthand
for Getting Things Done

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:44.357
became this global thing, kind
of like Kleenex and Xerox,

00:15:44.357 --> 00:15:45.501
and we didn't own it.

00:15:45.501 --> 00:15:47.885
I mean, we owned it, but
it was kind of running

00:15:47.885 --> 00:15:50.133
faster than us, and we
really had to rethink

00:15:50.133 --> 00:15:52.293
how are we showing up
out there in the world

00:15:52.293 --> 00:15:54.469
because people would meet me, or meet us

00:15:54.469 --> 00:15:56.341
and go, "Wow, you're nothing
like what I expected"

00:15:56.341 --> 00:15:57.414
"you to be."

00:15:57.414 --> 00:15:58.630
I said, "What did you expect me to be?"

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.157
They said, "Well,
corporate and left-brain"

00:16:00.157 --> 00:16:03.101
"and hard-working and
rigorous and disciplined"

00:16:03.101 --> 00:16:04.837
"and whatever," and a lot of people go,

00:16:04.837 --> 00:16:07.169
"You know, I probably
should but that's not me."

00:16:07.169 --> 00:16:08.849
Well, that's not us either,

00:16:08.849 --> 00:16:11.257
and so, there was a
disconnect between how we were

00:16:11.257 --> 00:16:13.075
actually showing up in the world,

00:16:13.075 --> 00:16:16.067
and people's perception
of us and the reality.

00:16:16.067 --> 00:16:20.055
We had a really smart guy
help us think through this,

00:16:20.055 --> 00:16:22.294
and it's really about being authentic.

00:16:22.294 --> 00:16:24.390
Those really tie together called

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:25.830
what's my signature?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:26.814
What's the David Allen signature?

00:16:26.814 --> 00:16:28.214
If you go to my website now,

00:16:28.214 --> 00:16:31.197
if anybody ever saw it a year or two ago,

00:16:31.197 --> 00:16:33.549
it looks very different
now than it did then

00:16:33.549 --> 00:16:35.132
because what we decided was,

00:16:35.132 --> 00:16:36.461
look, take the tie off,

00:16:36.461 --> 00:16:38.780
(laughs) you know, because I'm really

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:40.854
kind of a hang out, spontaneous, you know,

00:16:40.854 --> 00:16:42.356
kind of guy which is really a lot

00:16:42.356 --> 00:16:43.860
of what my methodology's about

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:45.664
and what the message is about.

00:16:45.664 --> 00:16:47.813
Initially, we had targeted the market

00:16:47.813 --> 00:16:49.140
of the people, those are the people,

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.716
the high-profile professionals

00:16:51.716 --> 00:16:53.580
and fast-track professionals were the ones

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.925
who were probably in the most pain

00:16:54.925 --> 00:16:56.076
in terms of overwhelm,

00:16:56.076 --> 00:16:57.805
and they could use the
methodology the most

00:16:57.805 --> 00:16:59.364
to begin with, but the truth is,

00:16:59.364 --> 00:17:00.637
it's for anybody.

00:17:00.637 --> 00:17:02.396
It's now spread around the world,

00:17:02.396 --> 00:17:03.702
and our signature,

00:17:03.702 --> 00:17:05.052
in other words, our expression

00:17:05.052 --> 00:17:07.253
is much more aligned
with who we really are.

00:17:07.253 --> 00:17:09.230
We really didn't have to go anywhere.

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:11.692
You know, many times the
problem companies have

00:17:11.692 --> 00:17:13.444
is their marketing is a big ta-da,

00:17:13.444 --> 00:17:15.857
and they can't deliver on the big ta-da.

00:17:15.857 --> 00:17:17.338
Well, our ta-da sucked.

00:17:17.338 --> 00:17:19.481
You know, we were delivering huge value,

00:17:19.481 --> 00:17:21.945
and people were having
transformational experiences,

00:17:21.945 --> 00:17:25.623
but you know, it didn't
look that way, you know.

00:17:25.623 --> 00:17:27.447
So we said there are a lot
of people we're not reaching

00:17:27.447 --> 00:17:29.351
because there's kind
of an inauthentic-ness

00:17:29.351 --> 00:17:30.919
about what we were doing.

00:17:30.919 --> 00:17:31.752
So we--

00:17:31.752 --> 00:17:32.585
- [Interviewer] That's been aligned now,

00:17:32.585 --> 00:17:34.032
with the new website and the new brand?

00:17:34.032 --> 00:17:36.480
- Yeah, yeah, much more so.

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.800
Whether it works as a
business, I don't know,

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.728
but it's certainly a
lot more fun (laughs).

00:17:40.728 --> 00:17:41.672
- [Interviewer] Okay, that totally

00:17:41.672 --> 00:17:42.672
makes sense.
- I don't have to show up

00:17:42.672 --> 00:17:43.680
and try to be somebody else,

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.777
or have to deal with
people's perception of me

00:17:45.777 --> 00:17:47.744
not being who I really am,

00:17:47.744 --> 00:17:49.625
so it may be more approachable,

00:17:49.625 --> 00:17:52.264
lowering the bar for people
to be able to engage,

00:17:52.264 --> 00:17:53.808
and to engage with me.

00:17:53.808 --> 00:17:54.752
You know, early on, you have to kind of,

00:17:54.752 --> 00:17:56.664
you know, everybody, you know, probably

00:17:56.664 --> 00:17:57.936
gets a nice business card

00:17:57.936 --> 00:17:59.345
so that you look like you're bigger

00:17:59.345 --> 00:18:01.153
than you probably really are.

00:18:01.153 --> 00:18:03.458
You know, you start to
create an image and a brand

00:18:03.458 --> 00:18:06.418
around who we think we really ought to be

00:18:06.418 --> 00:18:09.122
given so we can attract people,

00:18:09.122 --> 00:18:10.955
and not turn them off,

00:18:12.059 --> 00:18:13.578
but at some point, you
really need to kind of

00:18:13.578 --> 00:18:14.732
catch up with that,

00:18:14.732 --> 00:18:17.146
and allow yourself to just
kind of be who you are,

00:18:17.146 --> 00:18:18.186
and let the world come to you

00:18:18.186 --> 00:18:19.786
that are interested in you.

00:18:19.786 --> 00:18:20.777
- [Interviewer] Okay, makes sense.

00:18:20.777 --> 00:18:22.779
- But that's been as much

00:18:22.779 --> 00:18:24.442
a personal development development,

00:18:24.442 --> 00:18:26.946
as a marketing development on my side.

00:18:26.946 --> 00:18:28.033
- [Interviewer] Okay, that's fascinating,

00:18:28.033 --> 00:18:30.808
so, again, there's two
things happening here.

00:18:30.808 --> 00:18:32.960
As you develop in the
personal development,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.832
the marketing, those
two things are aligned,

00:18:34.832 --> 00:18:36.072
and they're important for them both

00:18:36.072 --> 00:18:38.345
to create a successful business.

00:18:38.345 --> 00:18:39.968
- I think so.

00:18:39.968 --> 00:18:42.568
You know, but I'm not ...

00:18:42.568 --> 00:18:44.536
I haven't studied all
the successful businesses

00:18:44.536 --> 00:18:46.160
to say that's how they did it.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:48.336
I do know that in the
world that we're in now

00:18:48.336 --> 00:18:49.960
because it's so transparent,

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:53.627
and social media can
spread word like crazy,

00:18:55.346 --> 00:18:58.074
and essentially that transparency,

00:18:58.074 --> 00:18:59.332
the more authentic you are,

00:18:59.332 --> 00:19:01.000
probably, the safer it's going to be,

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.777
so you don't have to, you know, worry

00:19:02.777 --> 00:19:04.536
about trying to be
something that you're not,

00:19:04.536 --> 00:19:06.016
or, "Gee, they thought of me as that,"

00:19:06.016 --> 00:19:07.632
"and now, I have to be that for them,"

00:19:07.632 --> 00:19:08.962
"and I have to be that for them--"

00:19:08.962 --> 00:19:10.050
- [Interviewer] It just makes life easier.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:11.584
- It does make life easier.

00:19:11.584 --> 00:19:13.048
Whether it makes it
more profitable or not,

00:19:13.048 --> 00:19:14.329
I would think so,

00:19:14.329 --> 00:19:15.496
but I, you know, I think the world

00:19:15.496 --> 00:19:17.464
gets attracted to authenticity.

00:19:17.464 --> 00:19:18.297
- [Interviewer] I agree.

00:19:18.297 --> 00:19:20.448
- That's, I think, where the world is

00:19:20.448 --> 00:19:21.808
because it's so transparent,

00:19:21.808 --> 00:19:24.725
in-authenticity, I think, shows up,

00:19:25.813 --> 00:19:27.637
at least subliminally if not directly.

00:19:27.637 --> 00:19:28.470
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.710
- You know, so, you know,

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.974
people out there are trying
to create marketing campaigns

00:19:31.974 --> 00:19:33.766
that really aren't who you are,

00:19:33.766 --> 00:19:35.087
are trying to show up as something

00:19:35.087 --> 00:19:37.198
that's just somebody's writing ad copy,

00:19:37.198 --> 00:19:39.638
but then, your engagement
with the company,

00:19:39.638 --> 00:19:41.470
you know, doesn't hold up to that,

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:43.413
or doesn't match to that,

00:19:43.413 --> 00:19:45.558
you know, that's tricky business.

00:19:45.558 --> 00:19:49.289
- Competition is one of the
greatest illusions ever created,

00:19:49.289 --> 00:19:51.652
but more so, something which keeps us

00:19:51.652 --> 00:19:53.403
out of our true authenticity.

00:19:53.403 --> 00:19:55.675
If I say I want to compete with you,

00:19:55.675 --> 00:19:57.035
compete with what,

00:19:57.035 --> 00:20:01.202
because you were born at
a different time than me,

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.991
you've got a different objective than me,

00:20:03.991 --> 00:20:07.724
and we aren't in the same time and space.

00:20:07.724 --> 00:20:09.237
(inhales)

00:20:09.237 --> 00:20:11.261
Instead of competition,

00:20:11.261 --> 00:20:13.543
think more of cooperation.

00:20:13.543 --> 00:20:15.771
That helps you become more authentic

00:20:15.771 --> 00:20:17.299
because you say, "I get it."

00:20:17.299 --> 00:20:19.578
"You are totally unique and weird,"

00:20:19.578 --> 00:20:20.588
"and guess what?"

00:20:20.588 --> 00:20:22.210
"I am totally unique and weird,"

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:24.294
"and now, we don't have
to go against each other."

00:20:24.294 --> 00:20:28.448
"We can work together,
and honor our uniqueness,"

00:20:28.448 --> 00:20:31.576
and then, you just (inhales), mellow out.

00:20:31.576 --> 00:20:33.712
- Self-Love is absolutely vital

00:20:33.712 --> 00:20:35.672
when being authentic,

00:20:35.672 --> 00:20:38.632
so it's taking the
shadow, the flaws of you,

00:20:38.632 --> 00:20:41.384
of that person that you are,

00:20:41.384 --> 00:20:42.888
and meshing it together with

00:20:42.888 --> 00:20:44.776
that infinite intelligence,

00:20:44.776 --> 00:20:46.488
that centered-ness, that connected-ness,

00:20:46.488 --> 00:20:47.960
that compassion, that love,

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.960
that light that you are,

00:20:51.677 --> 00:20:55.069
and going out into the world
and demonstrating that.

00:20:55.069 --> 00:20:57.133
It's all about the demonstration,

00:20:57.133 --> 00:20:59.973
and as you demonstrate more, my friend,

00:20:59.973 --> 00:21:01.701
the more people are
going to come up to you.

00:21:01.701 --> 00:21:03.564
They're going to see you as a catalyst

00:21:03.564 --> 00:21:05.124
for change in their own life,

00:21:05.124 --> 00:21:06.884
and you never know who
you're going to impact,

00:21:06.884 --> 00:21:08.756
but you've heard me talk about it before.

00:21:08.756 --> 00:21:10.060
It's that ripple effect,

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:13.074
so the more you and I
can become authentic,

00:21:13.074 --> 00:21:16.094
we can become in that state of flow,

00:21:16.094 --> 00:21:18.020
that state of awesomeness,
we could call it,

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.673
or that state of truly being authentic,

00:21:21.673 --> 00:21:24.649
everything else will change in your world.

00:21:24.649 --> 00:21:26.273
People are going to come
to you out of the woodwork

00:21:26.273 --> 00:21:28.730
asking you how you did it,

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.580
and that's when you can show them

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.348
how to be truly authentic,

00:21:32.348 --> 00:21:34.524
and really benefit and change their life,

00:21:34.524 --> 00:21:35.484
and that's what it's all about.

